Two open questions from all-21 (2026-11-18), both about things the log could not tell apart:
- The freeze after 117 minutes: kernel alive, no frame from backboardd any more, no error line. The USB command "status" now
  also says: vsync count and age of the last one, frames shown, display on/off, panel level; GPU ready, last fence submitted
  and completed, ring read/write pointers. Asked twice a few seconds apart it tells a dead vsync timer, a GPU that stands
  still and a window server that submits nothing from one another.
- Slow frames: backboardd's long glFlush (median 18 ms in 28 of 60 frames over 16.7 ms) falls into periods in which 3-5 MB
  a submission go out of the processor's cache under gGPULock. The five-second line now has two more: submissions, bytes
  pushed, push time and time waited for the lock, for backboardd and for everybody else, and the largest single push with
  its IOSurface.
Nothing changes what is drawn or when. Not run on hardware yet.

